<title>SWEDEN: Skanska 9-mo profit jumps on one-off gain.</title>
<headline>Skanska 9-mo profit jumps on one-off gain.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to Sept 30,</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 3,435  vs   2,049</p>
<p> Order bookings			  36,449  vs  27,355</p>
<p> Operating expenses		    32,211  vs  25,733</p>
<p> Capital gain on shrs sold	    1,760  vs	 4</p>
<p> Invoiced sales			  35,126  vs  28,941</p>
<p> Depreciation				 862  vs     733</p>
<p>Operating profit after</p>
<p>	 depreciation		     2,053  vs   2,475</p>
<p> Dividends				    488  vs     351</p>
<p> Net interest items		CHARGE 658  vs     694 CHARGE</p>
<p> Other financial items	     CHARGE 1  vs	 8 CHARGE</p>
<p> Taxes					  618  vs     553</p>
<p> Minorities				   109  vs     188</p>
<p> Net profit				 2,602  vs   1,308</p>
<p> Shr (crowns)				20.7  vs    10.4</p>
<p>NOTE -- Skanska is a Swedish construction and real estate group. The operating expenses include a 1.1 billion crown write-off for trademarks.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-7001017</p>
</text>
